incident-bot: :rotating_light: INCIDENT ALERT: Canary rollout for model redwood-text-2-canary in eu-west-1 showing elevated 5xx rate and tail latency. Auto-fallbacks triggering repeatedly. Paging @alice_oncall and @erin_sre. Please ack. alice_oncall: Acked. I'm on it — collecting quick logs and scope. Can someone drop the rollout config? bob_runtime: Copy — looking at runtime metrics. We're seeing error surge starting 11:30 UTC. KV cache misses + OOM-ish stack traces in the canary pods. Logs: ```2026-03-15T11:30:22Z service:model=redwood-text-2-canary region=eu-west-1 error=502 upstream=kv-cache OOM java.lang.OutOfMemoryError```

carol_platform: FYI the rollout policy for this canary is: ```{
  "strategy": "rolling",
  "canary_pct": 10,
  "regions": ["eu-west-1","us-west-2"],
  "fallback_policy": {"type":"sticky","sticky_ttl_sec":3600,"preferred_variant":"latest"}
}``` I think preferred_variant should've been "stable-quantized" but config says "latest" — that causes fallback to pick the canary variant instead of the older stable one. alice_oncall: That would explain why fallback loops back into canary in eu-west-1. So the "sticky" fallback is sticky to the variant label, not to a stable region. Can we pause the rollout and flip fallback to force-stable? dave_support: Noted — customers affected: SatoriPay (eu customers seeing elevated latency), AcmeAnalytics (partial failures on batch embeddings). I'll open an incident page for outreach. erin_sre: I'm running the mitigation playbook. Immediate steps: 1) pause canary 2) set fallback_policy to forced_variant: stable-quantized 3) drain canary pods in eu-west-1 4) monitor error-rate. alice_oncall: Executing step 1 now. CLI: `redwood rollout pause --id rlt-9a3f --region eu-west-1`

